# UI Reference Rules (cookapp)

## Prefer screenshots over recordings

- Design and implementation reference lives in `docs/ui-screenshots/`.
- Prefer reading those still screenshots over screen recordings / video when reconstructing UI.
- Do not ask to re-watch recordings if the needed screen already exists as a screenshot.

## Ignore device chrome (never recreate)

When reading screenshots for layout, styling, or implementation, **always ignore**:

1. **Status bar** — time, signal, Wi‑Fi, battery, etc.
2. **Dynamic Island / notch** — the pill or cutout at the top of the phone.
3. **Keyboard** — system or app keyboard overlays; they are not part of the screen design.

Do not implement, style, or account for these elements in the app UI. Treat content below the status bar / Dynamic Island and above any keyboard as the actual design surface.
